  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cbf87697",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This document contains all the results from and code used to complete the 'Pumpkins' portion of the LIFE4138 Coursework."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "da4dc23b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Task 1 - Read in the dataset 🔍\n",
    "The first task involved reading in the `pumpkins.csv` file. To do this the following `import_dataset` function was made."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "91406837",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#| echo: true\n",
    "#| code-fold: true\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "def import_dataset(path :str): \n",
    "    '''\n",
    "    Function to import a csv dataset from its filepath or url\n",
    "    Checks to see if \n",
    "    Arguments:\n",
    "    path: Takes a string of a url or filepath of a csv file to import.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns:\n",
    "    dataset - returns a pandas dataframe\n",
    "    '''\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        dataset = pd.read_csv(path)\n",
    "        print('Dataset imported successfully!')\n",
    "        return dataset\n",
    "    except FileNotFoundError:\n",
    "        print(\"File not found, please enter a valid path\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "52d4cb5d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This could then be called using the filepath of the .csv file. It is assigned here to the variable `pumpkins` for ease of use later."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "e4b6af02",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Dataset imported successfully!\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| echo: true\n",
    "pumpkins = import_dataset('pumpkins_datasets/pumpkins_02.csv')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "665bd690",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 2 - Identifying the heaviest pumpkin ⚖️\n",
    "Next was to identify the heaviest pumpkin and data about it including: weight, variety, where it was from and when it was grown.\n",
    "\n",
    "To do this the `find_highest` function was created to get the row with a highest value in a specific column.\n",
    "\n",
    "The code for this function can be seen here:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "e1740567",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#| code-fold: true\n",
    "#| echo: true\n",
    "def find_highest(dataframe: pd,column: str):\n",
    "    '''\n",
    "    Function to get the row information of the highest value in a column\n",
    "\n",
    "    Arguments:\n",
    "    dataframe: the dataframe to search through\n",
    "    column: the column to search through for the highest value\n",
    "    '''\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        highest_row = dataframe.loc[dataframe[column].idxmax()]\n",
    "        return highest_row\n",
    "    except KeyError:\n",
    "        print(\"Please use a valid column name\")\n",
    "    except NameError:\n",
    "        print('Please provide a valid variable')\n",
    "    except AttributeError:\n",
    "        print('Please enter a valid argument type')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0f5dc491",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This function was called and we can see general information about the pumpkin below."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "4cb13dd2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "The heaviest pumpkin was a Champion from Terricciola, Tuscany, Italy.\n",
      "It weighed 2727.22lbs and was grown in the year 2021.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| echo: true\n",
    "heaviest_pumpkin = find_highest(pumpkins,'weight_lbs')\n",
    "print(f\"The heaviest pumpkin was a {heaviest_pumpkin['variety']} from {heaviest_pumpkin['city']}, {heaviest_pumpkin['state_prov']}, {heaviest_pumpkin['country']}.\\nIt weighed {round(heaviest_pumpkin['weight_lbs'],2)}lbs and was grown in the year {heaviest_pumpkin['id'].removesuffix('-P')}.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cb08ad13",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 3 - Conversion and Creation 📏\n",
    "### Converting pounds to kilograms\n",
    "The function `lbs_to_kg` was created to convert a value in lbs to kg, allowing it to be applied on mass in the next part."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "ec872a34",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#| echo: true\n",
    "def lbs_to_kg(value: float|int) -> float:\n",
    "    '''\n",
    "    Function to convert a value in lbs to kg\n",
    "    Takes a column input of values in lbs\n",
    "\n",
    "    Arguments:\n",
    "    value: a value to be converted\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns: new value as a float\n",
    "    '''\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        return ((float(value))/2.20462) #return converted value\n",
    "    except:\n",
    "        print(\"Please enter a valid value\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f385a118",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We can test this works using known values of lbs and kgs. For example, 2.20462 lbs is equal to 1kg and running the function should return `1.0`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "f4b9f2f2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "1.0"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 1076,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| echo: true\n",
    "lbs_to_kg(2.20462)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3659022a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Creating a new column\n",
    "Now that this function is verified to work it can be used to create new column of weight in kilograms.\n",
    "\n",
    "The following line of code was ran that created a new column and called the previously created function"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "14754101",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#| echo: true\n",
    "pumpkins[f\"weight_in_kg\"] = [(lbs_to_kg(i)) for i in pumpkins['weight_lbs']] #Creates new column using values by calling conversion function in list"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ea31cc6e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now we can take a look at the new column in the dataset:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "d7d68d77",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "       id place  weight_lbs grower_name     city  state_prov        country  \\\n",
      "0  2018-P   594  1019.99016  Wolf, Andy  Olympia  Washington  United States   \n",
      "\n",
      "                               gpc_site    seed_mother pollinator_father  \\\n",
      "0  Baumans Farm Giant Pumpkin Weigh-off  1702 Sherwood              Self   \n",
      "\n",
      "          ott   est_weight  pct_chart variety  dataset_id  weight_in_kg  \n",
      "0  367.117268  1204.293958        0.0    Wolf           2    462.660304  \n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| echo: true\n",
    "print(pumpkins.head(1))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9513e4ae",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We can re-run the code from earlier on the new column to find the value in kg for the heaviest pumpkin"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "9b1e87b7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "The heaviest pumpkin was a Champion from Terricciola, Tuscany, Italy.\n",
      "It weighed 1237.05kg and was grown in the year 2021.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#|echo: true\n",
    "heaviest_pumpkin = find_highest(pumpkins,'weight_in_kg')\n",
    "print(f\"The heaviest pumpkin was a {heaviest_pumpkin['variety']} from {heaviest_pumpkin['city']}, {heaviest_pumpkin['state_prov']}, {heaviest_pumpkin['country']}.\\nIt weighed {round(heaviest_pumpkin['weight_in_kg'],2)}kg and was grown in the year {heaviest_pumpkin['id'].removesuffix('-P')}.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7386f3c4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 4 - Weight class 🏋🏼‍♂️\n",
    "This task required creating another new column, with three classes of weight: light, medium and heavy.\n",
    "\n",
    "The thresholds decided for these were as follows:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Threshold | Weight (kg) |\n",
    "|-----------|-------------|\n",
    "| light     | <250        |\n",
    "| medium    | 250-500     |\n",
    "| heavy     | >500        |\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "This column was created using the following code."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "dc683268",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#| echo: true\n",
    "classes = []\n",
    "for i in pumpkins['weight_in_kg']:\n",
    "    if i<250:\n",
    "        classes.append('light')\n",
    "    elif i<500:\n",
    "        classes.append('medium')\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        classes.append('heavy')\n",
    "pumpkins[\"weight_class\"] = classes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3127b4c4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We can see the `weight_class` values for the first three rows below"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "f6be4fd5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "   weight_in_kg weight_class\n",
      "0    462.660304       medium\n",
      "1    610.834010        heavy\n",
      "2    639.005502        heavy\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| echo: true\n",
    "print(pumpkins[['weight_in_kg','weight_class']].head(3))   "
   ]
  }
